# Tier 1 monitoring redesign (CLAUDE.md "Session update ... 2026-09-04,
# spec/playbook v76") — fires trading-bot-digest.service at 17:30
# America/New_York, weekdays only, 30 minutes after Track B/Track C's
# shared 17:00 America/New_York post-close slot so both daily jobs have
# finished first.
#
# UPDATE (follow-up decision, same session): the original implementation
# used a literal, fixed `21:30:00 UTC` OnCalendar= line, which this
# file's own prior header flagged as only a true 30-minute offset from
# the other two jobs' timezone-aware `17:00:00 America/New_York` schedule
# during Eastern Daylight Time — during Eastern Standard Time the digest
# would have fired 30 minutes BEFORE, not after, the daily jobs it's
# meant to follow. Resolved by switching to the same
# `America/New_York`-relative anchoring trading-bot-daily.timer /
# trading-bot-track-c.timer already use, eliminating the drift entirely
# rather than just documenting it. Droplet systemd is confirmed 255 (see
# CLAUDE.md "Current status", systemd-units milestone droplet-side
# verification) — comfortably past the >=239 this per-line OnCalendar=
# timezone syntax requires, so no new risk from this change.
#
# Requires systemd >= 239 for the per-line OnCalendar= timezone suffix —
# see trading-bot-daily.timer's header for the older-systemd fallback.
[Unit]
Description=Run trading-bot-digest.service every weekday, 30 minutes after the shared daily post-close slot

[Timer]
OnCalendar=Mon..Fri *-*-* 17:30:00 America/New_York
Persistent=false
AccuracySec=1min

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
